@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How to complete checks when the parent or guardian is an asylum seeker";
}

<div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
    <a class="govuk-back-link backLinkJS" href="@Url.Action("Guidance", "Home")">Back</a>

    <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
    <p>
        Some parents who are claiming asylum are eligible for free school meals under separate eligibility criteria.
        These families may not have a National insurance number and cannot be processed through our standard online free school meals
        checking system.
    </p>

    <p>
        To complete checks, local authorities should:
        <ul>
            <li>review supporting evidence to check an applicant with an asylum support reference number (formerly NASS number)</li>
            <li>only use the approved application form for asylum seekers if the applicant has been unable to provide supporting evidence for the local authority to check</li>
        </ul>
    </p>

    <div class="govuk-accordion" data-module="govuk-accordion" id="accordion-default">
        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-1">
                        Reviewing supporting evidence
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-1" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-1">
                <p class="govuk-body">
                    An applicant with an asylum support reference number (formerly NASS number) needs to provide a document proving they are receiving relevant support under part VI of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999. This may include:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>a letter from the Home Office</li>
                    <li>a visa or student visa</li>
                    <li>other kinds of documentation, to be reviewed at your discretion</li>
                </ul>

                <p>
                    If the document provided demonstrates that they receive such support, this is sufficient evidence for them to claim free school meals for their children.
                </p>
                <p>
                    There is another subset of failed asylum seekers supported under Section 4 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999, whose children may also be eligible for free school meals. For guidance, read <a target="_blank" href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/free-school-meals-guidance-for-schools-and-local-authorities/providing-free-school-meals-to-families-with-no-recourse-to-public-funds-nrpf">providing free school meals to families with no recourse to public funds (NRPF) on GOV.UK</a>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-2">
                        Accessing and completing the approved application form
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-2" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-2">
                <p class="govuk-body">Local authorities can use the approved offline free school meals application form for asylum seekers if the applicant has been unable to provide supporting evidence.</p>
                <p class="govuk-body">
                    This document is classified as <b>OFFICIAL-SENSITIVE</b>. Only authorised local authority
                    staff should access and complete it.
                </p>

                <p class="govuk-body">
                    <a target="_blank" href="~/documents/LA-request-form-for-asylum-seeker-checks.pdf">
                        Access the official free school meals application form (authorised users
                        only)
                    </a>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-3">
                        Where to send the completed form
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-3" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-3">
                <p>Completed forms should be sent to: <a target="_blank" href="ICESSVECWorkflow@homeoffice.gov.uk">ICESSVECWorkflow@homeoffice.gov.uk</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-4">
                        When to use the form
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-4" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-4">
                <p>Use the offline form when the parent or guardian:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>is seeking asylum</li>
                    <li>does not have a National insurance number</li>
                    <li>cannot provide supporting evidence for the local authority to check </li>
                    <li>cannot be verified through the online system</li>
                    <li>meets the free school meals criteria under asylum support arrangements</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-5">
                        How local authorities should support families
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-5" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-5">
                <p>You must:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>request supporting evidence confirming asylum support status</li>
                    <li>provide information about the offline form if the applicant cannot provide supporting evidence </li>
                    <li>ensure that the completed form is submitted to the Home Office for confirmation </li>
                    <li>communicate the outcome of the application to the family in a timely manner </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-6">
                        Submitting and storing the form
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-6" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-6">
                <p>
                    Local authorities must ensure that the offline form is submitted securely and stored appropriately. This includes:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>using secure methods to submit the form to the Home Office</li>
                    <li>keeping a copy of the submitted form and any supporting evidence</li>
                    <li>storing all documents securely to protect the family's privacy</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="govuk-accordion__section">
            <div class="govuk-accordion__section-header">
                <h2 class="govuk-accordion__section-heading">
                    <span class="govuk-accordion__section-button" id="accordion-default-heading-7">
                        Help and support
                    </span>
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div id="accordion-default-content-7" class="govuk-accordion__section-content"
                 aria-labelledby="accordion-default-heading-7">
                <p>For further help and support, contact our support team using the <a target="_blank" href="https://customerhelpportal.education.gov.uk/" class="govuk-link">Customer help portal</a>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>